<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Come Saturday, it will be 73 days since th=
e pain and shame of Atlanta, when England, from a winning position in a Wor=
ld Cup semi-final, decided to do an England, and sit on their lead. What fo=
llowed resembled a slow-motion crash test dummies video, Enzo Fern=C3=A1nde=
z first summoning the ghost of Andy M=C3=B6ller at Euro 96 with his high-ca=
mp cavorting celebration, and then Lautaro Mart=C3=ADnez, unmarked, nodding=
 home. Englishmen across the globe slumped, Croydon BoxPark fell deathly si=
lent. Allowing Lionel Messi the freedom of Georgia on the inside-right chan=
nel had turned out to be a critical oversight. Whoops.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Still too soon? Feels that way. An everlas=
ting international break brings unwelcome flashbacks to the summer, the Nat=
ions League quadruple-header a soft re-entry to international football, tho=
ugh facing world champions is a severe test of credentials. Any Football As=
sociation bloviation of a best performance since 1966 in winning a third-pl=
ace playoff game that resembled a hungover Soccer Aid, France not making a =
tackle in the first half, has done little to brush away the disappointment.=
 Plenty of blame to share around, and Thomas Tuchel more than happy to shar=
e it. His explanation for that battening down of the hatches has been a cas=
e of =E2=80=9Cit=E2=80=99s not me, it=E2=80=99s you=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Tuchel version of events is that shove=
lling on Big Dan Burn with nine minutes to play was a reaction to players h=
aving already decided unilaterally to bunch up in front of Jordan Pickford =
and follow in the tradition of failures past. Conjuring Sid Vicious=E2=80=
=99s thoughts on the man in the street, Tuchel has said 99% of fans don=E2=
=80=99t ask him about his Atlanta substitutions. To follow Tuchel=E2=80=99s=
 narrative, there=E2=80=99s some corner of a foreign field that=E2=80=99s f=
or ever an England player, exhausted, unable to complete a pass, gassing ou=
t. It is a compelling argument, plenty such cases to back it up, though was=
 it not Tuchel=E2=80=99s job to stop it happening? Analysis this week sugge=
sted the gassing out followed Tuchel asking players to run too hard in the =
group stage. A squad mostly coming off hard seasons in the grasp and grappl=
e of the Premier League could not replicate such energy in the knockouts, t=
heir rearguard efforts against Mexico and Norway portentous preludes to fac=
ing Argentina.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Entering a fantasy scenario, the likelihoo=
d is that Spain, who teased Argentina to the point of losing their rag, wou=
ld have done much the same to England in the final. They already did that i=
n the Euro 2024 final. Spain enjoying 21st century success often sends root=
-and-branch reformers to ask whether England can learn lessons. But =E2=80=
=9Cwe don=E2=80=99t have that strength like the Spanish, where we control g=
ames like they do,=E2=80=9D sighed Anthony Gordon, now playing in Spain, me=
mories of his goal in Atlanta bittersweet. Gordon=E2=80=99s solution? =E2=
=80=9CPlay to our strengths, which is play physical, play direct football a=
nd on the counterattack.=E2=80=9D Sounds familiar. With Tuchel unrepentant,=
 the English ready themselves for Euro 2028 as more of the same, starting S=
aturday with Spain.</p>
